^page{^T{Tracks}}{^empty}{^resourcesPrimary}{^tracksSecondary}{^cbox{^tbox{
^h1{^T{Tracks}}
^PAR{A Gauge 1 running track needs a lot of space - a free-running oval takes around 15m x 7.5m or 45 feet x 23 feet to allow for 3m radius curves. As a result most G1 tracks are outside, and G1MRA members usually join one or more or our ^link{local groups}{Groups^us^lang.html} to take advantage of invitations to run at members' homes.

The other way to find somewhere to run is to join a club with Gauge 1 interests: you'll find a list below.

G1MRA also has around a dozen ^em{portable} tracks (though 'transportable' might be a better term since a trailer is usually needed to move them around) and groups arrange running days for their members where a track is put up in a rented hall. Our portables also appear at many ^link{events}{Events^us^lang.html}.

^bf{If you are an exhibition organiser and would like to have a G1MRA track at your event, please contact the managing group using the links below, or for a general discussion please email our events coordinator as ^g1mail{events}.
}
}

