^PAR{^T{To order models and kits, please fill in} ^link{^bf{^T{this form}}}{^modelOrderForm}. ^T{Payment may be made by direct bank transfer or by PayPal (with a £2.00 supplement to cover PayPal fees); account details are on the form.

^hrule
^h1{G1MRA 75th anniversary tanker - £75}
^imageBar{^image{g1mraTanker1.jpg}{The G1MRA anniversary tanker}}{^image{g1mraTanker2.jpg}{The G1MRA anniversary tanker}}{^image{g1mraTanker3.jpg}{The G1MRA anniversary tanker}}

Made for us by Accucraft as a variant of their very successful 1:32 14-ton tanker model. The anniversary transfers can be removed with a bit of work if you want a plain tanker... Very nice runners. Last few remaining - order now before they are all gone.

^hrule
^h1{Greenly starter engine fully built and ready to run but unpainted - £250}
^imageBar{^image{ghostGreenly1.JPG}{Greenly RTR engine}}{^image{ghostGreenly2.JPG}{Greenly RTR engine}}{^image{ghostGreenly3.JPG}{Greenly RTR engine}}

This Greenly starter engine has full radio control with 'cruise control', a powerful 5-pole motor, a flickering firebox light and a smoke generator that puffs. The engine will run for a couple of hours on a single charge and can pull 30 axles at speed with ease. 

As a short wheelbase 0-4-0 it can traverse 60cm radius curves: perfect for going round the Christmas tree.
The model is designed for robustness and is ideal for youngsters, but in an industrial livery the engine does not look out of place on an exhibition Gauge One layout.

You can learn more about the design, and read a detailed build guide (which includes example liveries) on our ^link{^T{designs page}}{Designs^us^lang.html}.

^bf{Please note} that these ready-to-run engines are constructed by a team of volunteers at our occasional 'build days'. As a result stock levels are very variable, and when a batch is sold there may be a lead time of some weeks before we can supply you. As a result, please do place an order using ^link{^bf{^T{this form}}}{^modelOrderForm}, but ^bf{do not make a payment until we request it}.


^hrule
^h1{Greenly starter engine KIT - £150}
^imageBar{^image{kitGreenly1.jpg}{Greenly kit contents}}{^image{kitGreenly2.jpg}{An assembled gearbox}}{^image{kitGreenly3.jpg}{Battery fitting}}

These kits are assembled by a team of volunteers at our occasional 'build days'. As a result stock levels are very variable, and when a batch is sold there may be a lead time of some weeks before we can supply you. As a result, please do place an order using ^link{^bf{^T{this form}}}{^modelOrderForm}, but ^bf{do not make a payment until we request it}. 

The kit build requires soldering and assembly skills. 

You can learn more about the design, and read a detailed build guide on our ^link{^T{designs page}}{Designs^us^lang.html}.

^hrule
^h1{Wagon (unpainted) - coming soon - price to be confirmed}

^cbox{^image{ghostRCHWagon.JPG}{Forthcoming RCH wagon}}

This wagon comes as a single piece print which includes brake gear and axle boxes.You also receive two axles, four wheels and coupling hooks. The wheels are slipped onto the axle - built in sleeves set the back-to-back wheel spacing correctly. You then ease the axle into the axle boxes, and fit coupling hooks.

^hrule
^h1{Brake van (unpainted) - coming soon	 - price to be confirmed}

^cbox{^image{ghostBrakeVan.JPG}{Forthcoming BR brake van}}

This BR brake van comes as a single piece print which includes brake gear and axle boxes and handrails.You also receive two axles, four wheels and coupling hooks. The wheels are slipped onto the axle - built in sleeves set the back to back correctly. You then ease the axle into the axle boxes, and fit handrails and coupling hooks.

^hrule
}}}}}

